FlashRescue — IoT layer
=======================

The real-time sensing, risk-prediction and alerting tier. All services are
decoupled microservices that communicate only over MQTT.

Layout
------
  dev_broker.mjs           Local MQTT broker (TCP 1883 + WebSocket 9001)
  Simulation/              Physics-based sensor world (see Simulation/README.md)
  Publishers/
    sensor_sim.cjs         Sensor network driven by the physics simulation
    volunteer_sim.cjs      Volunteer GPS and velocity vectors
  Subscribers/
    risk_predictor.cjs     Risk grid, diffusion forecast, zone detection, A* routing
    alert_service.cjs      Alert generation, rate limiting, notification dispatch
  Visualization Dashboard/
    sim_inspector.html     Physics inspector: storm cells, CWC gauges, slopes,
                           early warning, node batteries, link health
    dashboard.html         Operational map: heatmap, volunteers, zones, routes
    crowd_validation.html  Standalone trust-scoring demo (not wired to MQTT)

Prerequisites
-------------
  Node.js 14+            (developed against Node 20)
  npm install            mqtt, plus aedes for the bundled dev broker

No Mosquitto install is needed: dev_broker.mjs serves both plain MQTT for the
Node services and MQTT-over-WebSocket for the browser, which cannot speak raw
MQTT over TCP.

Quick start (two terminals)
---------------------------
  Terminal 1   node IoT/dev_broker.mjs
  Terminal 2   node IoT/Publishers/sensor_sim.cjs --scenario assam_brahmaputra_flood
  Browser      open "IoT/Visualization Dashboard/sim_inspector.html"

The inspector needs only the broker and sensor_sim. It shows the physics
directly: drifting storm cells, river stage against CWC Warning/Danger/HFL,
slope pore pressure and I-D exceedance, urban ponding, cyclone pressure,
earthquake early-warning lead times, node batteries, and link loss.

Full stack
----------
  Terminal 1   node IoT/dev_broker.mjs
  Terminal 2   node IoT/Publishers/sensor_sim.cjs --scenario normal_monsoon
  Terminal 3   node IoT/Publishers/volunteer_sim.cjs
  Terminal 4   node IoT/Subscribers/risk_predictor.cjs
  Terminal 5   node IoT/Subscribers/alert_service.cjs
  Browser      open "IoT/Visualization Dashboard/dashboard.html"

To point a dashboard at a different broker, append it to the URL hash:
  sim_inspector.html#ws://192.168.1.50:9001

To inspect the simulation without a broker:

  node Publishers/sensor_sim.cjs --list
  node Publishers/sensor_sim.cjs --scenario sikkim_glof_2023 --headless

Scenarios outside the default Assam grid print the CENTER_LAT / LAT_SPAN
environment variables that risk_predictor.cjs needs so the risk grid covers the
sensors. For example:

  CENTER_LAT=27.7 CENTER_LON=88.45 LAT_SPAN=1.0 LON_SPAN=0.7 \
    node Subscribers/risk_predictor.cjs

Topics
------
  sensors/{node}/{kind}    risk-bearing readings (carry valueNorm)
  telemetry/{node}/{kind}  context readings (no risk weight)
  nodes/{node}/health      battery, drift, stuck sensors
  nodes/{node}/status      retained online/offline for dead-node detection
  events/seismic           earthquake records with early-warning lead times
  risk/grid                current risk grid
  risk/forecast            diffusion forecast steps
  risk/zone                detected high-risk zone polygons
  viz/vol_flow             aggregated volunteer flow vectors
  routes/request           evacuation route requests
  routes/{id}              computed routes
  alerts/{zoneId}          emitted alerts
  sim/world                simulation ground truth
  sim/events               scenario timeline narration
  sim/stats                node and transport statistics

Known gaps
----------
  - alert_service.cjs still depends on Twilio (paid). Replacement with
    self-hosted ntfy, Telegram, Web Push, CAP 1.2 emission and a LoRa mesh
    fallback tier is planned.
  - risk_predictor.cjs republishes the full 1600-cell grid as JSON every second.
    A binary quantised payload with a static geometry header is planned.
  - risk_predictor.cjs uses a single risk threshold and convex hulls; graded
    severity, concave hulls and a slow-trend channel for slow-onset hazards
    (Joshimath-style subsidence) are planned.
  - crowd_validation.html generates random mock reports and is not connected to
    the live sensor feed or the trust-fusion logic.
